J.A.I.S.S. (Just A Intelligent Secure System) - Major Architectural Milestone & System Optimization
Executive Summary
This release marks a major development sprint covering the full vertical stack of the J.A.I.S.S. custom AI architecture—from core model design and harness orchestration to runtime execution, automated deployment pipelines, and comprehensive local storage hygiene.

Core Engineering Milestones
1. Model Layer
Established the foundational architectural framework supporting modular gene-based weight representations and non-standard state routing.

Implemented decentralized state synchronization mechanisms designed to prevent drift across autonomous execution silos.

2. Harness Layer
Developed robust execution wrappers to manage model states, enforce zero-drift memory registers, and handle telemetry polling.

Integrated validation gates to monitor execution flow and maintain operational integrity.

3. Tools Layer
Engineered a suite of custom PowerShell utilities and automation daemons for workspace telemetry, deep storage auditing, and automated system maintenance.

Built modular verification scripts for rapid visual vault assessments and recovery point checks.

4. Runtime Layer
Configured local runtime environments optimized for tensor processing pathways and hardware acceleration support.

Streamlined local toolchain integrations and model weight caching directories for seamless inference execution.

5. Automated Release & Maintenance Pipeline
Established streamlined archiving workflows and automated clean-up gates to maintain repository and workspace hygiene.

System Optimization & Storage Hygiene
Local Temp & Package Cache Purge: Reclaimed ~2.9 GB by clearing stagnant temporary files and installer package caches.

Redundant Installer Cleanup: Wiped over 5.3 GB of heavy, executed setup binaries (including CUDA toolkits, driver packages, .NET SDKs, and old compressed archives) from local storage.

Cloud Vault & Telemetry Verification: Audited Google Drive and local vault directories, securing 52.49 GB of free headroom (52.5% available) while verifying 100% integrity across recovery checkpoints.
